    "PathBinder batch-ingest manifest. Consumed by ingest_missing_sets.py.",
    "One entry per TCGplayer group (set). Fields:",
    "  key         short handle used by --only (set_code also works)",
    "  enabled     false = listed for reference, skipped unless --include-disabled",
    "  game        catalog.game_type value (pokemon / yugioh / onepiece / lorcana / dbfusion / gundam / magic)",
    "  category    TCGplayer categoryId (verified by name against /tcgplayer/categories at run time)",
    "  category_name  expected category name, so a renumbered id fails loudly",
    "  group       TCGplayer groupId (explicit). Omit to resolve via group_match.",
    "  group_match all substrings must appear in the group name (case-insensitive); must hit exactly one group",
    "  set_code    catalog.set_code to assign (id becomes {prefix}-{set_code.lower()}-{card_number})",
    "  set_name    catalog.set_name — ALWAYS set explicitly. Leaving it to the importer is how the",
    "              JP M5/M6 rows ended up with set_name = 'M5' / 'M6'.",
    "  lang        JA for Japanese Pokemon (id prefix jp- instead of en-)",
    "  sealed      also import the group's sealed products (import_tcgcsv_set.py --sealed)",
    "  embed       run CLIP embeddings for the new singles (embed_catalog_rows.py --id-prefix)",
    "  released    informational",
    "Generated from new_sets_2026-09-15.md. Group ids verified live against tcgcsv.com on 2026-09-15."
